WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.667
The package.json file is the visible
contract for an npm project.

2
00:00:06.747 --> 00:00:11.904
It names the package, declares runtime
dependencies,

3
00:00:11.984 --> 00:00:18.599
development dependencies, scripts, package
manager expectations,

4
00:00:18.679 --> 00:00:23.276
and metadata used by developers and
automation.

5
00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:31.205
Security review should treat package.json
as more than a manifest of convenience.

6
00:00:31.285 --> 00:00:38.349
It defines what code can enter the project
and which commands can run during

7
00:00:38.429 --> 00:00:43.250
development, build, test, and release
workflows.

8
00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:50.394
The package-lock.json file captures the
resolved dependency tree for the

9
00:00:50.474 --> 00:00:51.819
application.

10
00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:59.411
It records specific package versions,
integrity values, registry locations,

11
00:00:59.491 --> 00:01:02.518
and transitive relationships.

12
00:01:02.598 --> 00:01:07.308
This does not prove that every dependency
is safe,

13
00:01:07.388 --> 00:01:13.106
but it does make the install more
repeatable and reviewable.

14
00:01:13.186 --> 00:01:15.540
When a lockfile changes,

15
00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:23.469
the team can see the actual dependency
movement instead of assuming a broad version

16
00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:27.697
range resolved to the same tree
everywhere.

17
00:01:27.777 --> 00:01:32.599
The node_modules directory is a generated
result,

18
00:01:32.679 --> 00:01:36.042
not a trustworthy source of record.

19
00:01:36.122 --> 00:01:39.486
It can be large, machine-specific,

20
00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:44.499
and easy to corrupt through local
experimentation.

21
00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:50.746
Secure teams usually review package.json
and lockfile changes,

22
00:01:50.826 --> 00:01:55.087
use repeatable installation in automation,

23
00:01:55.167 --> 00:02:00.661
and avoid relying on manually edited
installed packages.

24
00:02:00.741 --> 00:02:07.356
The important question is not just what is
present on one workstation,

25
00:02:07.436 --> 00:02:15.060
but what a clean install will reproduce in
CI and production build environments.
